ow substrings simultaneously: the canonical step name `- name: External live-Dokploy smoke tests`, the canonical run command `go test -run TestLiveDokploySmoke ./...`, the `workflow_dispatch:` trigger, the `schedule:` trigger, and the `YALLA_EXTERNAL_DOKPLOY: "1"` env injection. Pinning the env-injection literal is essential: without it, the smoke would t.Skip silently and the workflow would always report green without ever reaching Dokploy. Forward-applicable to every opt-in verification story: pin BOTH triggers AND the env-injection literal in the same matcher; the trigger + opt-in pair is what makes the workflow's nightly run actually exercise the gate. (3) `VERIFY.SH OPTIONAL STEP GATED ON THE SAME ENV VAR THE TEST READS AT RUNTIME` — the verify.sh step's `if [[ "${YALLA_EXTERNAL_DOKPLOY:-}" = "1" ]]; then` guard ensures the optional step is skipped on developer laptops without the opt-in, but exercises the identical command CI runs when the operator does opt in. The static test pins BOTH the canonical step header `# 29. Optional: external live-Dokploy smoke tests` AND the literal command `YALLA_EXTERNAL_DOKPLOY=1 go test -run TestLiveDokploySmoke ./...` — the leading env prefix is part of the contract because verify.sh's step header is a comment, not an env-injection line, so the env prefix MUST appear in the command itself. Forward-applicable to every opt-in verification story: gate the verify.sh optional step on the SAME env var the test reads at runtime and pin the env-prefixed command literal as part of the contract. (4) `CONTRIBUTING.md ENTRY LIVES IN A NEW "Opt-in external suites" SUBSECTION UNDER THE EXISTING OPTIONAL TOOLS BLOCK, NOT THE NUMBERED REQUIRED LIST` — the numbered required list (1-24 after BE-0399) is reserved for the on-every-PR gates; opt-in suites get a separate subsection so contributors see the cadence boundary at a glance. The static test pins only the canonical entry literal (the command with surrounding backticks) so the analyser is 